INT. VILLA TERRACE - DUSK

A hilltop villa in the Italian lakes. Terracotta pots spilling bougainvillea. Fairy lights strung between lemon trees. Below, the lake lies like polished pewter. A long table is laid for a wedding rehearsal dinner.

At the head of it, SIGNORA CATERINA BELLINI-OKORO, 60s, in emerald silk, directs two waiters with small, imperious flicks of her wrist. Beside her sits her daughter, the bride-to-be, FRANCESCA "FRANCIE" BELLINI-OKORO, 28, in a cream wrap, twisting a glass.

The groom, HARLAN "HARL" ACHEBE-LINDQVIST, 30, rakish in rolled sleeves, leans back with a grin. His best man, THEO FAIRWEATHER-KOWALCZYK, 31, ties a napkin round his own head as a joke. Harl's mother, MRS. PERPETUA ACHEBE-LINDQVIST, 55, small, hawk-eyed, sits upright, her handbag clutched on her lap. And last, perched on the balustrade like a bird, is Francie's friend ROSALIND "TILDA" ODUYA-HART, 28, bridesmaid, sandals dangling.

CATERINA
Glasses!

Everyone obeys. Waiters pour prosecco.

HARL
Francie, my love.

FRANCIE
My love.

THEO
(muffled by napkin)
I object.

TILDA
Theo, you're not the officiant.

THEO
I'm practising.

PERPETUA
Harlan. Sit up straight.

HARL
Mama, I am.

PERPETUA
You slouch like your father.

CATERINA
Perpetua, a toast!

PERPETUA
I don't make toasts.

CATERINA
Then I will.

She rises. Everyone else half-rises in sympathy and sinks again.

CATERINA (CONT'D)
To my daughter, and to this boy who has the grace to look frightened.

HARL
I'm not frightened.

THEO
You're a little frightened.

TILDA
You're green.

HARL
It's the lighting.

Francie reaches for his hand. Harl takes it. They are both smiling too widely. Perpetua studies them over the rim of her glass.

PERPETUA
(dry)
Marriage is a long road.

CATERINA
And a longer lunch.

The table laughs. The tension lifts. Then, from the villa's terrace door, a clatter.

A caterer's tray crashes. Cannoli skid across the stones. Everyone turns.

In the doorway stands a man in a white jacket, a stranger, looking stricken. Behind him a second tray tilts, shuddering.

THEO
Everyone, down!

Chaos. Theo dives under the table with his napkin still on his head. Tilda leaps off the balustrade. Perpetua rises, handbag swinging like a flail. Caterina barks at the waiters. Francie and Harl, startled, collapse into each other, upsetting a candelabrum. Prosecco sprays. The caterer drops to his knees, scrabbling for pastry.

CATERINA (CONT'D)
(over the din)
Enough! Enough!

Silence falls. A single cannolo rolls to a stop at Perpetua's foot.

She picks it up. Examines it. Bites.

PERPETUA
(chewing)
Not bad.

The terrace erupts in laughter. Harl kisses Francie. Tilda applauds. Theo emerges from under the table, napkin crooked.

THEO
Did I miss the vows?

CATERINA
Not yet, caro. Sit.

The waiters refill glasses. The lights twinkle. Below them, the lake darkens, and one by one, the lamps of the far shore come on.
